      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you really sure? I looked at one, and e.g. `i915_gem_dmabuf_mmap` calls `vfs_mmap`, which I believe sets the fault handler to `shmem_fault`, which does in fact access `vm_file`.\n\nOr any of the GPU drivers that use TTM use `ttm_bo_vm_open` as the open callback, which uses `vma-\u003evm_file-\u003ef_mapping`.",
